<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">Changelog 2026-08-19 — Hermes Branch Context: authoring guideline + status correction</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-19 | Version: 0.1 | Tracked in project:
        <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">What changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Authoring guideline added (new §3.3).</strong> <a href="/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan" class="doc-link">HermesBranchContextPlan</a> now has a concrete "How to build a branch <code>.hermes.md</code>" recipe: exact file path (<code>~/.comserv/worktrees/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv/.hermes.md</code>, the worktree git root), the MANDATORY global-pointer header (point to <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/.hermes.md</code> — do NOT copy rules), required Branch identity / domain / worktree-rules blocks, port-from-worktrees.json rule, and a 4-point post-create verification (incl. asserting the GLOBAL file is unchanged).</li>
                <li><strong>Status correction.</strong> The prior plan asserted the branch <code>.hermes.md</code> files were "DONE" on 2026-08-17. They did NOT exist on disk then. The 7 active worktree files (planning, InventoryAccounting, 3d, DockerHA, ai, aichatsystem-ef4e, git) were actually created 2026-08-19 with the §3.3 template. The <code>planning</code> branch (missing from the original list of 6) is now included.</li>
                <li><strong>Incident recorded.</strong> A batch-seeding step overwrote the GLOBAL <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/.hermes.md</code> with a branch template; it was detected and the original 104-line global content restored verbatim. §3.3.4 + the §3.3 gotcha now forbid iterating over <code>main</code> with the branch template — the global path is read-only.</li>
                <li><strong>Plan bumped</strong> to page_version 0.2; todo 2142 gate text corrected; MASTER_PLAN nav + index already cross-link this doc (no change needed there).</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="doc-h2">Why</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The user needs a repeatable, mistake-proof way to give every branch its own Hermes context so an agent working in a worktree knows which branch it is on and keeps all global conventions. The earlier plan described the WHY and domain notes but gave no build recipe, and falsely claimed completion — which is exactly how the branch files ended up missing and a global file got clobbered. §3.3 closes both gaps.</p>

            <h2 class="doc-h2">Related</h2>
